.Dd September 13, 2026
.Dt ZKEYS.TOML 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm zkeys.toml
.Nd configuration file for zkeys
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
file configures the
.Xr zkeys 8
client.
.Pp
This file is TOML-formatted and its main purpose is to define a table of keys
available for retrieval.
.Sh FORMAT
The following example shows a typical configuration file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
service_url = "https://zkeys.jmmv.dev/"

[keys.sample]
id = "01234567-89ab-cdef-0123-4567890abcde"
remote_password = "foo"
local_secret = "baz"
.Ed
.Ss Security
The configuration file contains the remote passwords used to retrieve keys and
may contain a local portion of a secret.
Restrict read access to the file to the account that runs
.Nm zkeys .
.Ss Top-level settings
.Bl -tag -width XXXX
.It Va service_url
URL of the zkeys service.
The URL must not contain a path.
.Pp
Default:
.Dq https://zkeys.jmmv.dev/
.El
.Ss Keys
Each key is declared in a
.Va keys . Ns Ar name
table, where
.Ar name
is the local name passed to
.Cm zkeys get-key .
Each table must contain the following settings:
.Bl -tag -width XXXX
.It Va id
The UUID that identifies the key to the zkeys service.
.It Va remote_password
The password required to retrieve the key from the remote service.
.It Va local_secret
The local portion of the secret (not known by the service), prepended to the secret
returned by the service.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr zkeys 8
.Sh AUTHORS
The
.Nm
package was developed by
.An Julio Merino
.Aq julio@meroh.net .
